id: pm-extension-read-output-controls
title: Let SDK extension read commands opt into universal context output controls
description: "Real calendar adoption for PR1439 exposed an enhancement opportunity: the optional read command correctly omits universal output-budget flags from its contract, and the core guard refuses them because read-output policies currently enumerate built-in surfaces. Add an explicit public SDK declaration and structured output contract allowing package authors to opt read commands into projection, omission and budget controls while preserving fail-closed behavior for writers and undeclared commands. Current calendar JSON behavior and shipped core read controls remain valid."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-11T08:48:09.560Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-13T01:16:58.097Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-13T00:57:45.514Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-13T00:57:45.514Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: Installed Node and Bun read extensions opt in through a public SDK contract and preserve omission and budget refusal semantics; write and undeclared extension commands continue to reject read-only controls; aliases agree with availability and flag contracts.
parent: pm-xp1xsw
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "Added validated immutable read_output declarations, shared SDK shaping and continuation, canonical extension identities, native dispatch protection, action-precedence alignment, custom-flag-preserving schema discovery and authoring documentation."
expected_result: "Installed npm/Bun package readers reuse truthful universal controls across CLI, SDK and MCP; undeclared writers refuse controls and native behavior remains intact."
actual_result: "10327 tests pass; all786 measured files have exact100/100/100/100 coverage with zero gaps. Full static gates, linked tests, public contracts/types and npx/bunx smoke pass. npm/Bun installed consumers verify all200 rows exactly once across bounded continuation. Source implementation is complete; hosted delivery and registry publication are independently verified."
